      'print.estimate': 'Estimate from the Bambu Studio slicer on an X1 Carbon with these settings, without the supports under the three bosses of the body: PETG about 7 hours and 120 g, TPU about half an hour and 4 g. The real time depends on the printer and the speeds.',
      'print.how.title': 'How to print',
      'print.how.orient': 'Every file already lies in the right position, nothing needs rotating in the slicer: the arc is printed flat on the bed, the button cap upside down, the top face down.',
      'print.how.supports': 'Supports are needed only in the body. In Bambu Studio paint them by hand (“Paint-on supports”) under the three bosses for the bottom screws: they are the lugs on the inner wall near the bottom. Places the printer bridges across do not need supports.',
      'print.how.layer': 'Print the PETG parts with a 0.16 mm layer: the height of the ring arcs is fitted to a body printed that way. With a thinner layer (for example 0.12 mm) the arcs come out 0.04 mm lower than the bridges: the top then rests on the bridges and the arcs rattle.',
